STARTER Debugger
================

Interactive CLI debugger for starter-core. Attaches to the optional remote
debug server (`org.starter.Core.Debug`) exposed when core is built with
`--enable-debug-server`.

Build
-----

    ./autogen.sh
    ./configure
    make
    sudo make install

Requires: GLib/GIO, flex, bison, libreadline.

Tests
-----

    make check

`test/test-debugger` drives the session and CLI against an in-process mock
of `org.starter.Core.Debug` (no live starter-core required).

Usage
-----

Start starter-core with the debug server enabled, then:

    starter-debugger
    starter-debugger --core=127.0.0.1:17373

Default attach address is 127.0.0.1:17373.

At the `(starter)` prompt:

    help
    status
    info peers | info io [FILTER] | info vars [FILTER]
    info break | info watch
    monitor [all|on|off]
    monitor inputs|outputs|io|stats|vars|peers|stopped [on|off]
    break ID | watch ID
    delete break HANDLE | delete watch HANDLE
    continue
    set input ID = VALUE | set output ID = VALUE
    source examples/session.stdbg
    quit

`info io` / `info vars` show values observed via debug signals since attach
(there is no full I/O snapshot method on the core debug interface yet).

Breakpoints pause before rule apply for an id; watchpoints pause on value change.
Use `continue` after a `Stopped` event.

Command history is stored in ~/.starter-debugger_history.

